\section{Results}
\FloatBarrier
\subsection{The broad arrangement is shared more than the detail}
Models agree strongly about the arrangement of group centres. With 256 papers per centre, mean corrected CKA is 0.939 for the 26 areas and 0.911 for 217 specialties (Figure~\ref{fig:scales}A). Using only 26 specialty centres gives 0.902. Random groups matched in size and dates also agree to some extent, around 0.63--0.64, but fall below the observed groups. Averaging contributes to the comparison without fully accounting for the agreement associated with the area labels.
\PanelFigure{figure_01}{Agreement about area summaries and the papers inside them. Higher corrected CKA means greater agreement between models. (A) Mean agreement between group centres, each formed from 256 papers. Random groups preserve sizes and dates; the 26-specialty condition also matches the number of centres. (B) Agreement within groups at three article counts, using 26 areas and the same 183 specialties. Points and labels show means. Lines cover the 2.5th--97.5th percentiles of group--model-pair comparisons: 1,170 for areas and 8,235 for specialties. They show the spread of those results, not confidence intervals. Model pairs share models and are not independent. Both axes span 0--1; the panels compare different objects, not a causal effect of scale.}{scales}{1}

